<p>Taiwanese President Lai Ching-te arrived in Eswatini on May 2 to visit Taipei’s only diplomatic ally in Africa after his April itinerary was postponed when several overflight permissions were withdrawn. Taiwan said the failed route resulted from Chinese pressure on Indian Ocean countries, while Beijing called the eventual trip a political maneuver rather than legitimate diplomacy. Lai met King Mswati III, and Taiwanese public media said the two sides signed a customs mutual assistance pact and a joint communiqué. Beijing criticized the visit, while Taipei said Taiwan has the right to conduct official overseas visits.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qmagXfNhYhqx-2HkdtIA4npR_ZMChT_gIGnjcdohnbW7WP_1NJRYAOGXbPCJailD5oohqrmE8UDLsm_zccb-DD-ELWFZYtvjZj3fS1FGhAmyA8trXFjVS1VNt-OBCzaeR30--WIcFuNKoIv7zCo2eb0s-5B1Q7e0t7fvbDVOrU2Ceg7WxXsj0fOCEZTa3qAp23xEviTubA2Sh9ThOoEnS_a0tCBsbrCWI8ziPb9OEAEbZiPvHSsyDhRT2VE2aZxF' alt='Taiwanese President Lai Ching-te during his Eswatini visit.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Airspace decisions: Taiwan identified Seychelles, Mauritius and Madagascar as the states that withdrew permission; Taiwanese sources said the cancellations came without advance notice before the planned April 22-27 itinerary.</li><li>ATA precedent: Taiwan’s Foreign Ministry described Lai’s eventual trip as an “arrive then announce” arrangement, and Taiwanese reports said officials cited past trips by U.S. presidents George W. Bush, Barack Obama, Donald Trump and Joe Biden as precedents.</li><li>Diplomatic allies: Eswatini is one of 12 states that maintain formal diplomatic relations with Taipei, a group concentrated mainly in Latin America, the Caribbean and the Pacific.</li><li>Beijing position: China’s Foreign Ministry told Eswatini and other countries to follow what it called the one-China principle and said Taiwan is part of China.</li></ul><blockquote>The Republic of China, Taiwan, is a sovereign nation and a Taiwan that belongs to the world - Lai Ching-te</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lai Ching-te: In his arrival message, Lai thanked Eswatini for supporting Taiwan despite diplomatic pressure and said the delayed delegation still received a warm welcome. (<a href='https://news.pts.org.tw/article/806446'>PTS</a>)</li><li>China’s Taiwan Affairs Office: The office said Lai’s claimed diplomatic achievements were gimmicks and would make him a laughingstock. (<a href='https://news.rthk.hk/rthk/ch/component/k2/1853313-20260502.htm'>RTHK</a>)</li><li>Taiwan Ministry of Foreign Affairs: The ministry said Beijing’s comments showed a lack of understanding of international diplomacy and that Taiwan’s overseas visits follow international rules and diplomatic practice. (<a href='https://www.mirrordaily.news/story/58755'>Mirror Daily</a>)</li><li>Taiwan Mainland Affairs Council: The council responded to Beijing’s criticism by saying the president of the Republic of China does not need approval from the People’s Republic of China to go anywhere. (<a href='https://news.nextapple.com/politics/20260503/69A73430B1F288FA6C21509509CEDA7C'>Next Apple News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/taiwan-president-defiant-as-begins-eswatini-trip-china-calls-him-a-rat/article70934580.ece'>Taiwan President defiant as begins Eswatini trip; China calls him a &#x27;rat&#x27;</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/02/g-s1-119911/taiwans-lai-lands-in-eswatini-in-a-trip-delayed-by-lack-of-overflight-clearance'>Taiwan&#x27;s Lai lands in Eswatini in a trip delayed by lack of overflight clearance</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/3/taiwan-leader-visits-eswatini-despite-chinas-attempts-to-block-trip'>Taiwan leader visits Eswatini despite China’s attempts to block trip</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c809ln029ldo'>Taiwan president visits Eswatini days after blaming China for cancelled trip</a